From ebe89415908e9fc1b826d3b9dace122db65f71d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marks-jhojan <153632015+marks-jhojan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:31:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] runtime: UNDS game state for U1 (health, weapon,
 ammunition, shots, damage)

Callbacks in U1's code (player update, WeaponController PostJointUpdate and
Fire, Player::EventHandler damage branch) publish:
  gs   health x1000, injured, weapon slot and type id, clip/reserve/size, grenades
  shot one round fired by the player's weapon
  dmg  damage type, amount, health before, source and player position/rotation
Handed to the loader only for U1 (BB_EXE), with UNDS_EVENTS set and
UNDS_STATE not 0.

The sites are found by instruction patterns (0.3.7+ loader): RIP-relative
displacements, call targets and the two instructions the Infinite Health /
Ammo cheats rewrite are wildcards. Each pattern matches once in U1 1.00
(eboot sha256 74cf17ba...) at the offsets verified by disassembly
(0x2645f0, 0x71e920, 0x71affe, 0x261eea), also with both cheats applied,
and none in U2 1.00. U1 1.02 is the same code with other displacements
(untested). The damage callback reads r15 from the thunk's saved registers
(no naked stub any more). Pointers kept between calls are read with
ReadProcessMemory / process_vm_readv. UNDS version 0.4.1.
Tests: tests/test_unds.c (objects laid out like U1 1.00's; pattern syntax).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
